        "original_id": "129149b7-b1ef-51b0-a424-3ef3d8d7c15a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hugo Pinell, Willie Tate, Johnny Larry Spain, David Johnson, Fleeta Drumgo, Luis Talamantez, George Jackson, W.L. Nolen\n- Organizations: San Quentin Six, Black Guerrilla Family\n- Places: San Quentin State Prison, California, Marin County\n- Events: August 21, 1971 escape attempt\n\nFacts:\n- In 1966, George Jackson and W.L. Nolen founded the Black Guerrilla Family while they were incarcerated at San Quentin State Prison in Marin County, California.\n- The Black Guerrilla Family is an African-American prison and street gang also known as the BGF, the Black Family, and the Black Vanguard.\n- On August 21, 1971, an escape attempt at San Quentin State Prison left six people dead, including George Jackson.\n- George Jackson was a co-founder of the Black Guerrilla Family.\n- The San Quentin Six were six inmates at San Quentin State Prison in California: Hugo Pinell, Willie Tate, Johnny Larry Spain, David Johnson, Fleeta Drumgo, and Luis Talamantez.\n- The San Quentin Six were accused of participating in the August 21, 1971 escape attempt at San Quentin State Prison.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
